## What this predicate means

**A `provides-method-for` B** — pattern/protocol A provides the methodology that artifact B used.  Dagger inverse of `uses-method-in` — where `uses-method-in` is the artifact-side assertion ("this memoir employed pattern X's methodology"), `provides-method-for` is the methodology-side assertion ("pattern X provides the methodology that these memorials used").  Per `protocol/predicate_lifecycle.md` §"Edge assertion is one-sided", the canonical asserted direction is the artifact side (`uses-method-in:`); `provides-method-for:` is derivable via inverse-of entailment and exists for vocabulary completeness + reverse-direction retrieval ("show every memoir that used pattern X's methodology").

